WEBVTT

00:14:57.496 --> 00:15:00.932
that about six months into the marriage
or a year, a couple years,

00:15:00.956 --> 00:15:04.146
you realize that the person you married
who seemed so perfect

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:06.580
is actually selfish in all sorts of ways.

00:15:06.604 --> 00:15:09.103
And as you're making
this decision about him or her,

00:15:09.127 --> 00:15:10.911
she's making this decision about you.

00:15:10.935 --> 00:15:12.163
So you have two choices.

00:15:12.187 --> 00:15:14.105
You can either have a truce marriage,

00:15:14.129 --> 00:15:16.845
in which you both sort of agree
to ignore the selfishness,

00:15:16.869 --> 00:15:20.997
or you can say, "Actually,
my selfishness is the key problem here."

00:15:21.021 --> 00:15:24.237
We all have a tendency to think
it's the other person's selfishness,

00:15:24.261 --> 00:15:26.937
but it's only our selfishness
that we can really control,

00:15:26.961 --> 00:15:30.124
and if both partners agree to declare war
on their own selfishness,